title: Keywords shadow method names after Dot (P0-10)
status: pending
atomic: true
priority: high
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-10T03:27:57'
updated_at: '2026-06-10T03:27:57'
result: ''
description: 'Method calls like `.send()`, `.close()`, `.count()`, `.query()`, `.set()`,
  `.insert()`, `.delete()` fail to parse because the lexer promotes those keywords
  unconditionally even after a `.`. Fix: in the lexer/parser, do not emit keyword
  tokens after a Dot — treat them as identifiers in that position. Audit all affected
  identifiers: send, close, count, query, view, set, insert, delete, and any others
  that appear as builtin method names. Add conformance tests: `ch.send(v)`, `ch.close()`,
  `store.query(...)` etc. must all parse. (review/14_findings.md P0-10, review/15_roadmap.md
  A.5)'
